\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sb100\sa100\f0\fs28\cf1\b TJ DARLEY CONSTRUCTION, LLC\par
\cf0\fs22\b0\b STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE (SOP): INTEGRATED BID PIPELINE\b0\par
\cf3\fs18 Version 2.4 - Operational Training Manual\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\f1\fs22\par
This guide details how to seamlessly flow data through our digital pipeline: from initial \b Ballpark Calculations\b0 , to the certified \b Client Pre-Bid Intake\b0 , onto the auto-populated \b Multi-Phase Bid Compiler\b0 , and finally generating a formatted \b Client Proposal Agreement\b0 .\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf1\b\fs24 STEP 1: INITIAL CRUNCHING IN THE BALLPARK ESTIMATOR\cf0\b0\fs22\par
The pipeline starts when a property owner calls requesting an excavation or site prep quote.\par
\bullet  \b Access the Ballpark Estimator\b0  tab on the main screen.\par
\bullet  Input proposed physical dimensions: \b Length of Excavation\b0  (feet), \b Top Width\b0  (feet), \b Bottom Width\b0  (feet), and \b Average Depth\b0  (feet).\par
\bullet  Apply soil and site factors: \b Soil Profile\b0  (clay, rocky, sand) and \b Site Access Quality\b0  (easy, moderate, difficult).\par
\bullet  Note the calculated outputs: \b Excavation Volumes in Cubic Yards (CY)\b0  and \b Surface Area in Square Feet/Acres\b0 .\par
\bullet  Use the \b "Copy Excel/Sheets Row"\b0  or \b "Copy Material Metrics"\b0  actions if you want to store these raw metrics on your office clipboard for administrative record-keeping.\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf1\b\fs24 STEP 2: LOGGING THE CLIENT PRE-BID FIELD INTAKE SURVEY\cf0\b0\fs22\par
Once the project moves forward into active planning, lock this surveyor data into browser database memory.\par
\bullet  Click the \b "Client Pre-Bid Intake"\b0  link located in the application header.\par
\bullet  Populate Client Profile details: \b Client Name\b0  (e.g., John Smith), \b Job Name\b0  (e.g., private pond & house pad), and \b Site Location\b0  Address.\par
\bullet  Assign the supervisor \b Foreman\b0  managing the field crew.\par
\bullet  Input the exact metrics (Length, Widths, Depth, Soil, Access) from your Ballpark Estimator calculations.\par
\bullet  Click \b "Submit Client Intake Report"\b0 . This secures the report and logs a unique \b Field Intake ID (FI_ID)\b0  in browser memory (\b tjd_client_intakes\b0 ) for instant preloading.\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf1\b\fs24 STEP 3: PRELOADING INTO THE MULTI-PHASE BID COMPILER\cf0\b0\fs22\par
This is the automated mapping engine that ties the pipeline together directly.\par
\bullet  Navigate to the \b Multi-Phase Bids\b0  tab in the applet.\par
\bullet  Find the header selector titled \b "Preload From Previous Pre-Bid Intake History"\b0 .\par
\bullet  Select your logged Client Job entry from the list.\par
\bullet  \b Dynamic Automation Trigger\b0 : Selecting the intake immediately executes our subsurface mapping algorithms. It sets your geometries and automatically pre-populates \b 6 standard project phases\b0  complete with customized material counts, labor hours, operator metrics, and heavy equipment fuel rates adjusted for your volumes.\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf1\b\fs24 STEP 4: EDITING AND FINE-TUNING ACTIVE ESTIMATES\cf0\b0\fs22\par
Verify local details and customize pricing variables:\par
\bullet  In the Project Totals summary list, identify any auto-populated subphase that needs custom tweaking.\par
\bullet  Click the \b "Edit"\b0  button (amber button with an editor icon) directly on that subphase card.\par
\bullet  The workspace shifts into \b Subphase Active Edit Mode\b0 . The live slider, equipment rate matrices, and subcontractor toggle keys pull back up to allow local overrides.\par
\bullet  Make your desired adjustments (such as adding subcontractor lump sums or overriding operator hours).\par
\bullet  Under the itemization summary tables, click \b "Save Edited Sub-Phase Changes\b0 ". The compilation sheets will update instantly to show your new margins.\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf1\b\fs24 STEP 5: GENERATING AND PRINTING THE CLIENT PROPOSAL\cf0\b0\fs22\par
Compile the agreement details and print/save to PDF:\par
\bullet  Review total accumulated variables: Materials cost, Operator labor, Fuel overheads, Subcontractor costs, and Company Markup.\par
\bullet  Add custom notes and site liability/blasting exclusion disclaimers in the \b Notes / Disclaimers\b0  field.\par
\bullet  Click \b "Print Proposal"\b0  at the bottom.\par
\bullet  Your device's printer dialog will open instantly. Adjust settings to \b "Save as PDF"\b0  to store a beautifully branded, high-contrast TJ Darley Construction, LLC bid invoice directly on your phone or desktop, ready to print or email to the client.\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf1\b\fs24 QUICK TIPS FOR CELL PHONE USER SHORTCUTS\cf0\b0\fs22\par
To make accessing this platform on your smartphone simple, click the \b TJ Darley logo badge\b0  in the header bar of the app to open the \b Cell Phone Shortcut Link Portal\b0 . Point your smartphone's camera at the QR code, load the site, and tap \b "Add to Home Screen"\b0  to save this app directly to your mobile desktop. This bypasses copy-pasting links every time you start an estimate!\par
}
